      {
        "id": 53429,
        "name": "Ameena",
        "username": "Ameena",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/ameena/{size}/1907_2.png",
        "created_at": "2013-02-24T18:31:40.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>You have to be careful, also, about when he flips - the damage he takes from the victims in the Safehouse is dealt by himself. Since he's taking that damage, it means he's flipping, and since he's flipping, it means he's got all five drugs out. Which means whatever damage total you come to, it's then increased by one (from the drug that boosts his damage) but also reduced by H-2 (from the drug that gives him that much soak the first time he takes damage that turn). Twice now we've been silly and had Tachyon hit him with a Hypersonic Assault (targets dealt damage by it can't deal damage till the start of Tachyon's next turn), which means that on flipping he deals himself <span class=\"bbcode-i\">no</span> damage from the Safehouse :P.</p>\n<p>Generally a good tactic against Spite is to have Wraith, armed with two Stun Bolts and a Utility Belt, double-Stun Bolt him every turn to nerf all his damage by two. If you've got someone like Legacy around to redirect and/or soak damage as well, you can pretty much nerf just about everything he does once flipped. He can be a wuss, but then again sometimes he can totally kick your arse, especially if he gets the damaging drugs out early. Once he flips, though, since he no longer draws cards you know exactly what he's going to do every turn so can set up to deal with it.</p>",
        "post_number": 4,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T02:27:36.677Z",
